The main saving is calling `GetType()` once and reusing the result. In the FIT SDK it is typically a virtual getter, and the original called it twice on the non-string path.

I also replaced the generic division by `baseTypeSizes` with shifts for the sizes 1, 2, 4 and 8. Any other size still uses plain division, so the result is identical.

This assumes `GetType()` has no side effects and returns the same value each time. That holds for the SDK's getter.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 FieldBase::GetNumValues(void) const
{
    if (!IsValid())
        return 0;

    const FIT_UINT8 type = GetType();

    if (type != FIT_BASE_TYPE_STRING)
    {
        const size_t n = values.size();
        const FIT_UINT8 sz = baseTypeSizes[type & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK];
        switch (sz)
        {
        case 1:
            return (FIT_UINT8)n;
        case 2:
            return (FIT_UINT8)(n >> 1);
        case 4:
            return (FIT_UINT8)(n >> 2);
        case 8:
            return (FIT_UINT8)(n >> 3);
        default:
            return (FIT_UINT8)(n / sz);
        }
    }

    return (FIT_UINT8)stringIndexes.size();
}
```